{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-be2f649e538bc508","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7fffcf48e81a7dc","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"planner: verify STORY-setup-001a plan","prompt":"You are an expert planning specialist focused on creating comprehensive, actionable implementation plans.\n\n## Your Role\n\n- Analyze requirements and create detailed implementation plans\n- Break down complex features into manageable steps\n- Identify dependencies and potential risks\n- Suggest optimal implementation order\n- Consider edge cases and error scenarios\n\n## Planning Process\n\n### 1. Requirements Analysis\n- Understand the feature request completely\n- Ask clarifying questions if needed\n- Identify success criteria\n- List assumptions and constraints\n\n### 2. Architecture Review\n- Analyze existing codebase structure\n- Identify affected components\n- Review similar implementations\n- Consider reusable patterns\n\n### 3. Step Breakdown\nCreate detailed steps with:\n- Clear, specific actions\n- File paths and locations\n- Dependencies between steps\n- Estimated complexity\n- Potential risks\n\n### 4. Implementation Order\n- Prioritize by dependencies\n- Group related changes\n- Minimize context switching\n- Enable incremental testing\n\n## Plan Format\n\n```markdown\n# Implementation Plan: [Feature Name]\n\n## Overview\n[2-3 sentence summary]\n\n## Requirements\n- [Requirement 1]\n- [Requirement 2]\n\n## Architecture Changes\n- [Change 1: file path and description]\n\n## Implementation Steps\n### Phase 1: [Phase Name]\n1. **[Step Name]** (File: path/to/file.ts)\n   - Action: Specific action to take\n   - Why: Reason for this step\n   - Dependencies: None / Requires step X\n   - Risk: Low/Medium/High\n\n## Testing Strategy\n- Unit tests: [files to test]\n- Integration tests: [flows to test]\n- E2E tests: [user journeys to test]\n\n## Risks & Mitigations\n- **Risk**: [Description]\n  - Mitigation: [How to address]\n\n## Success Criteria\n- [ ] Criterion 1\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n1. Be Specific: use exact file paths\n2. Consider Edge Cases\n3. Minimize Changes: prefer extending existing code over rewriting\n4. Maintain Patterns: follow existing project conventions\n5. Enable Testing\n6. Think Incrementally: each step must be verifiable\n7. Document Decisions\n\n## Red Flags to Check\n- Missing tests\n- Steps without clear file paths\n- Phases that cannot be delivered independently\n\nA great plan is specific, actionable, and considers both the happy path and edge cases.\n\n---\n\n# TASK (READ-ONLY PLAN VERIFICATION — you must NOT write or edit any files)\n\nWorking directory: /home/nitin-sharma/ralph-workspaces/6896163a-932b-4b96-bfe9-cdbb022c3538/c7df6267-784a-460a-addd-6d781a21b6f5\n(cwds persist; if needed, `cd` there at the start of any command.)\n\n## Current Story\n\nStory ID: STORY-setup-001a\nTitle: Create Root NextMove package.json With Workspaces\n\nDescription: Create the root package.json for the NextMove monorepo declaring npm workspaces over apps/*, pinned npm and Node 22.x versions, turbo 2.x devDependency, and turbo run scripts.\n\nAcceptance Criteria:\n1. Root package.json exists with name \"nextmove\", private: true, workspaces array containing \"apps/*\", packageManager pinned to npm@10, and engines.node \"22.x\".\n2. devDependencies pin turbo 2.x and scripts define build, test, and lint as \"turbo run build\", \"turbo run test\", \"turbo run lint\".\n3. The scaffold files are committed to the existing git repository with git commands exiting 0.\n\n## Known State from the Orchestrator (verify, don't trust blindly)\n\nA previous attempt already implemented this story before its session died (retry context):\n- `package.json` at repo root exists and is committed at HEAD. Reported content: name \"nextmove\", private true, workspaces [\"apps/*\"], packageManager \"npm@10\", engines.node \"22.x\", devDependencies.turbo \"^2.5.0\", scripts build/t